---
title: The opportunity page
description: The tabs and fields of an opportunity, moving it to another stage, changing the person in charge, and winning, losing or cancelling a deal.
sidebar:
  order: 4
---

Select a card on the board to open the opportunity. The row at the top shows the client (or that it is still a bare lead without a client), the **PERSON IN CHARGE**, the expected revenue, the probability, the expected close date, and how long it has been in its stage.

## The tabs

| Tab | Contents |
|---|---|
| **Details** | The stage bar and all fields of the opportunity (below). |
| **Services** | The services and prices picked for the deal. See [3 · Pick services and prices](/en/crm/pick-services/). |
| **Contract** | The contracts of the deal. See [4 · Prepare the contract](/en/crm/prepare/) and the chapters after it. |
| **Invoices** | The invoices raised for this opportunity. See [Invoices](/en/invoices/overview/). |
| **Files** | The files of the deal. See [9 · Opportunity files](/en/crm/files/). |
| **Timeline** | Notes about the deal. Select **Post a Note** to add one; type @ to notify a colleague. Notes can have attachments. |
| **Activity** | Every change to the opportunity's fields, with who made it and when. |

## The fields

Select a field to change it. On **Details**:

| Section | Fields |
|---|---|
| **Basics** | Lead number, opportunity name, contact person, **Manager in charge**, **Director in charge**, priority (0 to 3 stars). |
| **Money & forecast** | Expected revenue (or not quoted yet), probability and expected close. The expected close date is a forecast, not a deadline: nothing reminds you of it. The weighted forecast is the expected revenue × the probability. |
| **Classification** | Lead type, source, market, referred by, and the outcome reason of a lost or cancelled deal. The market is the country of the work, not the client's registered address. |

The client can be changed to another company or person already in **Clients**.

## Move to another stage

Select a stage on the stage bar, or drag the card on the board. In both cases the **Move to …** dialog asks for a **Note** saying what changed. The note is required: it is what makes the history of the deal readable later.

When the deal moves to **Lost** or **Cancelled**, also choose a **Reason** — why it did not close. **Lost** means the quote was beaten or refused; **Cancelled** means the client walked away. If no reasons have been set up, a team lead can add them (see [Stages and vocabularies](/en/crm/stages/#vocabularies)). If the deal is put back in play later, the outcome reason is cleared.

### Won

An opportunity cannot be marked won while any of its contracts is neither signed nor void. Operon then says how many contracts are not signed, with an **Open** link to each. Get the contract signed, or void it, and move the deal again. See [7 · Send for e-signature](/en/crm/e-signature/) and [8 · Paper signing, void and copy](/en/crm/paper-void-copy/).

When the deal is won or lost, its files move to the client's folder. See [10 · Close the deal](/en/crm/close-deal/).

## Change the person in charge

Change the **PERSON IN CHARGE** at the top of the page. Operon asks for a **Reason** — why the deal is changing hands — before the change is saved. The same applies to removing the person in charge.

The Manager in charge is notified when they are put on an opportunity.
